join detective right
detective: [NIECE], I have come to the conclusion that this will is fake.
join niece left
niece: Whatever do you mean?
detective: You’re not Dracula’s real heiress. 
detective: That title belongs to [FRIEND].
detective: I discovered that the guard was secretly a vampire all along.
detective: Meaning they are beholden to the vampires' rule of invitation.
detective: Dracula would have been the only one allowed to bring them in. That is, until he was killed.
detective: After Dracula's death, that ability transfers to his real heir.
detective: According to both of your accounts, [GUARD] did not come into the house when you invited them, even after Dracula’s death.
detective: If you were really Dracula’s heiress, the guard would have been able to enter the house with your invitation.
detective: However, they only entered after [FRIEND] invited them in, meaning that he is the real heir.
detective: Therefore, this will is a fake, and you must have planted it.
niece (disappointed): Preposterous!
niece: …
niece (speaking): You’re a clever one, I’ll give you that much.
niece: That will is fake. I forged it and hid it in his safe.
niece (disappointed): But I deserve to be his heiress!
niece (speaking): It should be someone from his own family, not some irrelevant friend!
join detective_thinking right
detective_thinking: She must have stolen the key to unlock the safe.
